Think: For each filename in manifest.txt, check if employees/<file> exists; create/overwrite missing_files.log to start empty; copy existing files to temp_workspace/{id}_raw.txt while recording missing names to missing_files.log — all done in one awk command.

Act: bash

```bash
awk 'BEGIN { miss="temp_workspace/missing_files.log"; print "" > miss }
{ file="employees/" $0; id=$0; sub(/\.txt$/, "", id);
  cmdtest = "[ -f \"" file "\" ]";
  if (system(cmdtest) == 0) {
    cmd = "cp \"" file "\" \"temp_workspace/" id "_raw.txt\"";
    system(cmd)
  } else {
    print $0 >> "temp_workspace/missing_files.log"
  }
}' temp_workspace/manifest.txt
```

