Think: For each file listed in temp_workspace/file_list.txt, extract tokens allowing an optional leading minus and sequences of letters/digits, and write them to per-file token files under temp_workspace/tokens using awk to process all files in one command.

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
  fname=$0;
  n=split(fname,a,"/");
  base=a[n];
  out="temp_workspace/tokens/tokens_" base;
  while((getline line < fname) > 0) {
    pos=1;
    while(match(substr(line,pos), /-?[A-Za-z0-9]+/)) {
      tok=substr(line, pos+RSTART-1, RLENGTH);
      print tok >> out;
      pos += RSTART + RLENGTH - 1;
    }
  }
  close(out);
}' temp_workspace/file_list.txt
```

