Think: Normalize epoch timestamps in raw_timestamps.csv to ISO8601 (UTC) while preserving paths (which may contain commas) and save results to normalized_timestamps.csv.

Act: bash

```bash
gawk '{
  if (match($0, /,[^,]*$/)) {
    sep = RSTART;
    path = substr($0, 1, sep-1);
    ts = substr($0, sep+1);
    printf("%s,%s\n", path, strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", ts));
  }
}' usr_scan_workspace/raw_timestamps.csv > usr_scan_workspace/normalized_timestamps.csv
